          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              is
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-excisive
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              (or
              %em polynomial
              of degree at most
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a strongly cocartesian
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n + 1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cube"} cube
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StronglyCoCartesian"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X)
              is a cartesian cube in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Cartesian"}
            %p
              A 1-excisive (∞,1)-functor is often just called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} excisive (∞,1)-functor
              for short.
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            is also called a
            %strong polynomial (∞,1)-functor
            (not to be confused with
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} other concepts having the same name
            %strong
              degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            when the smallest value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            for which it is
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This notion is comparable to how a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
              of degree at most
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is determined by its values on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n + 1
              distinct points.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#nExcisiveApproximation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-Excisive approximation and reflection
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} finite (∞,1)-colimits
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie-differentiable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} Goodwillie-differentiable (∞,1)-category
          #InclusionOfNExcisive.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Exc
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Exc^n(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D})
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Func(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D})
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-functor (∞,1)-category
              on those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
              which are
              = succeed "-excisive." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #nExcisiveApproximations.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The inclusion of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfNExcisive"}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} lex
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Exc
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P_n \;\colon\; Func(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}) \longrightarrow
                    Exc^n(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D})
            %p
              which moreover is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} left exact
              (preserves
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
          %p
            This is essentially the statement of (
            %a{:href => "#Goodwillie03"}> Goodwillie 03, theorem 1.8
            ). In the above form it appears explicitly as (
            %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"}> Lurie, theorem 6.1.1.10
            ). The construction of the reflector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_n
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"}> Lurie, constrution 6.1.1.27
            ).
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            this reflection is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrification"} spectrification
          %p
          #nExcisiveFunctorsFormInfinityTopos.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-excisive functors form an
                = succeed "-topos)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %br/
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} = \mathbf{H}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Exc
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Exc^n(\mathcal{C}, \mathbf{H}) \in (\infty,1)Topos
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n  \gt 1
              this is in general
              %em not
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercomplete+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} hypercomplete (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              is.)
            %p
          %p
            This observation is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"} Lurie, remark 6.1.1.11
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+locus"} Joyal locus
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              of definition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Exc
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Exc^n(\mathcal{C}, \mathbf{H}) \hookrightarrow PSh(\mathcal{C}^{op}, \mathbf{H})
              is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weiss+topology"} Weiss topology
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              As
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              ranges, the tower of
              = succeed "-excisive" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-functor," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#nExcisiveApproximations"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogous
              to the the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+series"} Taylor series
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie-Taylor+tower"} Goodwillie-Taylor tower
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 0
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to P_{n+1} F \to P_n F \to \cdots \to P_1 F \to P_0 F
                    \\,.
            %p
              If this converges to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is analogous to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+function"} analytic function
              and is called an
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} analytic (∞,1)-functor
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              In the situation of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#nExcisiveApproximations"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{n-1}F \simeq \ast
              (hence the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{n-1}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-modal+types"} anti-modal types
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} reduced (∞,1)-functors
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"} Lurie, def. 6.1.2.1
          %h3#homogeneous_pieces Homogeneous pieces
          %p
            A polynomial
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            — that is, a
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\lt k
            — is a
            %strong homogeneous
            polynomial if its approximation by an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-1)
            degree polynomial is trivial.
          %p (…)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} finite (∞,1)-colimits
              and with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} terninal object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+category"} pointed
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie-differentiable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} Goodwillie-differentiable (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              Then for all natural numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              composition with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/} \to \mathcal{C}
              induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Homog
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Homog
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Homog^n(\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D}) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} Homog^n(\mathcal{C}^{\ast/}, \mathcal{D})
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"}> Lurie, prop. 6.1.2.11
            )
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#GoodwillienJets
            Goodwillie
            = succeed "-jets" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+homotopy+types"} finite homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} finite (∞,1)-colimits
            from the point. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            finite homotopy types.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              we have that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Exc
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mi fin
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Exc^0(\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/},\mathbf{H}) \simeq \mathbf{H}
                  is the collection of constant functors, hence the original
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
                  itself;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Exc
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mi fin
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi T
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Exc^1(\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/},\mathbf{H}) \simeq T\mathbf{H}
                  is the collection of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %p Hence one might refer to the tower of toposes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi n
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mn 2
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to J^n \mathbf{H} \to \cdots \to J^2 \mathbf{H} \to T \mathbf{H} \to \mathbf{H}
            %p with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi n
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi Exc
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J^n \mathbf{H} \coloneqq Exc^n(\infty Grpd^{\ast/}, \mathbf{H})
            %p
              the tower of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} jet (∞,1)-categories
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            see (
            %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"}> Lurie, def. 1.4.2.8 and around p. 823
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} excisive (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie calculus
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie-Taylor+tower"} Goodwillie-Taylor tower
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} analytic (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} polynomial (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+n-excisive+functors"} model structure for n-excisive functors
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Goodwillie"}> Thomas Goodwillie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Calculus II, Analytic functors
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+tower"} Taylor tower
            formed by
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li#Goodwillie03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Goodwillie"}> Thomas Goodwillie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Calculus III: Taylor Series
              %strong 7
              (2003) 645-711 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0310481"}> arXiv:math/0310481
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2003.7.645"} doi:10.2140/gt.2003.7.645
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Rezk08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  A streamlined proof of Goodwillie’s
                  = succeed "-excisive" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %strong 13
              (2013) 1049-1051 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.1324"}> arXiv:0812.1324
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2013.13.1049"} doi:10.2140/agt.2013.13.1049
          %p
            A discussion in the general abstract context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#HigherAlg
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 6.1.1 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+n-excisive+functors"} model structure for n-excisive functors
            is given in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Biedermann"}> Georg Biedermann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Chorny"} Boris Chorny
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculus of functors and model categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0601221"} arXiv:math/0601221
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Biedermann"}> Georg Biedermann
                , Oliver Röndigs,
                %em Calculus of functors and model categories II
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1305.2834v2"}> arXiv:1305.2834v2
                )
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+Glasman"}> Saul Glasman
              ,
              %em Goodwillie calculus and Mackey functors
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.03127"}> arXiv:1610.03127
              )
